  "narrative": "No claims are currently due for assessment, and the accepted set remains empty. The accumulated evidence has been dominated by near-null or incoherent high-prevalence binary main effects, and prior independent validation has failed for H1, H36, H70, H77, and H85. The immediate registered priority remains the active feature_051 median-split interaction screen H170-H181, which tests common binary markers against the low-noise outcome family outcome_004, outcome_009, outcome_010, and outcome_003. To pre-specify the next contingent exploration without displacing that active screen, I register a focused interaction screen using the continuous age-like feature_061. The hypothesis is that an older or higher-feature_061 context modifies the association of the balanced binary marker feature_034 with dependency scores. Eligibility restricts to observed feature_061 values, while the subgroup feature_061 >= 54 defines the high-age context relative to observed feature_061 < 54. With direction -1, the claim is that the raw interaction is negative: relative to the lower-age complement, feature_034-exposed subjects in the higher-age context have a more negative dependency score, i.e., stronger dependency. I test four stable dependency outcomes, outcome_012, outcome_005, outcome_015, and outcome_002, whose means are near -0.25 and SDs are near 0.17-0.18; a 10% relative practical difference is therefore approximately 0.025 absolute dependency-score units. I would consider these results for follow-up only if the signed interaction estimates are near or above this threshold, their intervals exclude null and opposite/subclinical values, and the direction is coherent across the four outcomes. Plausible alternatives are that feature_061 does not modify feature_034-associated dependency, that the modification is opposite in sign, or that any apparent signal reflects median-split/missing-age selection or noise. If the screen is null or incoherent, this family should be closed without validation. If coherent, it would merit independent validation before acceptance. These are dataset-specific observational associations only and do not establish causality or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted set remains empty. Validated failures: H1, H36, H70, H77, H85. feature_010 >= 0 interaction screen H154-H165 was null/incoherent; feature_040 interactions H166-H169 closed as low-prior redundant. Current active/final-priority screen: H170-H181, feature_051 median split interacting with feature_002/feature_034/feature_060 on outcome_004/009/010/003. Registered contingent next screen: feature_034 interactions with feature_061 >= 54 among observed feature_061, tested on outcome_012/005/015/002. These new proposals are contingent and should not displace H170-H181 unless that active screen is completed and null. Acceptance bar: for stable outcomes, signed estimate about >=0.025, interval excludes null and opposite/subclinical values, coherence across outcomes; otherwise close without validation. Avoid further noisy main-effect or rare-cell screens unless a coherent threshold-level signal appears. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations only."
